@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title sbx virtiofs drops the agent's cwd — a silent Bash tool, and the two answers

' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/defaults/hooks/cwd-guard.sh, packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh,
'         internal/run/run.go, internal/run/helpers.go, internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go,
'         internal/sbx/run.go, cmd/proveo/main.go, internal/workspace/mount.go,
'         cmd/proveo/main_test.go, e2e/resume_test.go
'
' Measured 2026-09-01 on proveo-1787956302-22788 (proveo/claudecode, Claude Code
' 2.1.251), see the memory sbx-virtiofs-unlinks-agent-cwd for the full forensics.

participant "Host checkout\nsame inode throughout" as HOST <<host>>
participant "sbx microVM\nvirtiofs passthrough" as VFS <<cloud>>
participant "Claude Code\ncwd = workspace root" as CC <<app>>
participant "Bash tool spawn" as BASH <<error>>
participant "cwd-guard.sh\nPreToolUse(Bash)" as HOOK <<app>>
participant "proveo run\nclone by default" as RUN <<app>>

HOST ARROW_CLOUD VFS : workspace shared at its host path
VFS ARROW_ERROR CC : guest dentry unlinked;\nhost directory unchanged
CC ARROW_MAIN CC : cwd recorded as\n""<ws> (deleted)""
CC ARROW_ERROR BASH : every spawn: exit 1, no output\n(""true"" too, subagents too)
CC ARROW_OPTIONAL HOOK : hooks still spawn — Claude Code\nfalls back to the session start dir
HOOK ARROW_MAIN CC : exit 2: names the cause, forbids\nretries, asks for a restart
RUN ARROW_MAIN VFS : clone mode — the workspace lives\non the VM disk, not on virtiofs
RUN ARROW_MAIN HOST : teardown: snapshot + fetch to\n""refs/proveo/<sid>/*"" before ""sbx rm""
RUN ARROW_MAIN VFS : teardown save: ""sbx exec -w /"" —\nnever the container WorkingDir

note over HOST, VFS
  **The host did nothing.** Birth time and inode of the
  directory never changed; ""stat -L /proc/<pid>/cwd""
  still reached that inode. Only the guest's name for
  it was gone. No mount row in the audit log either:
  ""sbx exec"" re-evaluates policy, it does not remount.
end note

note over CC
  **Read/Edit/Write survive, Bash does not.** File tools
  take absolute paths; the Bash tool takes the cwd, and
  Claude Code ≥ 2.1.119 rejects a vanished one instead
  of falling back (anthropics/claude-code#52747). The
  model then blames the harness — which is what it saw.
end note

note over HOOK
  **Why a hook can speak when Bash cannot.** Claude Code
  spawns hooks from the session start dir when the cwd
  is gone, so ""PreToolUse(Bash)"" runs exactly when the
  tool would fail. Exit 2 puts stderr in front of the
  model. Silent on a healthy shell; ""PROVEO_CWD_GUARD=off"".
end note

note over RUN
  **Clone is the default, with named fallbacks.** sbx
  clones only a repository's MAIN worktree offered as
  the primary workspace: no repo, a linked worktree, a
  monorepo sub-scope, or the docker backend fall back to
  the mounted checkout and say why. Explicit ""--clone""
  there is an error; ""--clone=false"" / ""PROVEO_CLONE=off"" opt out.
end note

note over RUN, HOST
  **A clone dies with its VM.** ""sbx rm"" drops the in-VM
  clone and its ""sandbox-<name>"" remote, and removing a
  remote deletes ""refs/remotes/<remote>/*"". Teardown
  therefore commits what the agent left uncommitted,
  then fetches every branch into ""refs/proveo/<sid>/*"".
end note

note over RUN, VFS
  **Nothing may be mounted UNDER the repository in clone
  mode.** sbx mounts each positional workspace at its own
  host path and clones only into an EMPTY workspace. The
  harness's output dir (""<repo>/reports"") went to sbx as a
  second positional, landed inside the clone target first,
  and sbx skipped the clone without a word: the agent started
  in a root-owned directory holding nothing but ""reports/"",
  with the checkout read-only at ""/run/sandbox/source""
  (proveo-1788366117-41470, 2026-09-02; reproduced with a
  throwaway repo). ""SplitNested"" drops every nested bind and
  says so; the output dir is **lifted at teardown** instead —
  ""CloneLiftArgs"" tars it out of the clone over ""sbx exec""
  (stdio is forwarded) and the host unpacks it under the
  repo root, before the commit fetch. The ""--print"" plan
  never showed the nested positional because it does not
  create the output dir and non-existent hosts are dropped;
  ""e2e/clone_output_test.go"" drives ""proveo run"" itself.
end note

note over RUN
  **Teardown is an exec too.** ""SaveStateArgs"" pins ""-w /"":
  without it the copy-out inherits the dead WorkingDir and
  dies with the same ""getcwd"" error, exit 127, before a byte
  moves — "resume state not preserved" — and ""sbx rm"" then
  takes the volumes. Measured on 22788 at the end of a
  four-day session; the transcripts never reached the host.
  Reproduced on demand by replacing the workspace directory's
  inode on the host (""mv"" + ""mkdir""); putting it back does
  not heal the guest, only a restart does.
end note

note over BASH
  **Forensics.** ""sbx exec -w / <sb> -- readlink /proc/<pid>/cwd""
  — the ""-w /"" is load-bearing, the default workdir IS
  the broken directory and dies with
  ""getcwd: Operation not permitted"". The transcript's
  own ""cwd"" field carries the same "(deleted)" string.
end note
@enduml
